[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://ui/tutorial/tutorial_entry.gd" id="1"]

[resource]
script = ExtResource("1")
title = "Time System"
brief_tooltip = "Survive 365+ days until rescue arrives.
Seasons: Summer (mild) → Winter (deadly) → Spring (rescue)
Space: Pause | 1/2/3: Speed controls"
implemented = true
detailed_text = "[b]Survive Until Rescue[/b]

[i]The real expedition was abandoned by the Admiralty for over a year before search parties were sent. Your men must endure a full arctic cycle — summer, the long winter, and into the following spring — before any help can reach them.[/i]

Your goal is to keep as many men alive as possible until rescue arrives, over a year from now.

[b]Seasons[/b]

[b]Summer[/b] (Jun-Aug) — The mildest season. Long daylight hours. Use this time to prepare.
[b]Autumn[/b] (Sep-Nov) — Temperatures drop sharply. Last chance to build shelter before winter.
[b]Winter[/b] (Dec-Feb) — Brutally cold, short days, frequent blizzards. The killing season.
[b]Spring[/b] (Mar-May) — Slowly warming. Days lengthen. Rescue draws nearer.

Temperatures also shift with the time of day — warmer at midday, colder at night. Storms make it worse still.

[b]Speed Controls[/b]

[b]Space[/b] — Pause the game to plan without time passing
[b]1[/b] — Normal speed
[b]2[/b] — Double speed
[b]3[/b] — Quadruple speed

Speed up during quiet stretches. Pause when a crisis hits.

[b]Rescue[/b]

Rescue arrives after roughly 13-18 months. You will receive a warning when 30 days remain. Everything you do — every tent built, every barrel of food rationed — is buying time until that day comes."
